# UI Kit — `@f0rge/ui`

## Four layers (never skip or fork)

1. **Tokens** — semantic map in `libs/ui/src/styles/tokens.css`; brand skins in `libs/ui/src/styles/skins/*.css`. Apps `@import` a skin from `globals.css`. Brand vars (`--marrow-*`, `--dk-*`) live in skin CSS only — never in TSX.
2. **Composition** — app screens and domain widgets (Bristol grid, meal chips, symptom picker).
3. **Wrappers** — `libs/ui/src/components/ui/*`; engines stay inside this package.
4. **Documented overrides** — `libs/ui/src/styles/extras.css` only; never edit `node_modules` or fork engine internals.

## App imports (hard ban)

Apps import **only**:

- `@f0rge/ui` — primitives, `cn`, date formatters, hooks
- `@f0rge/ui/forms` — labeled data-entry (Mantine wrappers)
- `@f0rge/ui/api` — marrow API client only; dk keeps its own axios client

**Never** in `apps/**`:

- `@base-ui/react`
- `@mantine/core`, `@mantine/hooks`, or any `@mantine/*`

## Engines (libs/ui only)

`@base-ui/react` and `@mantine/*` are implementation details of `libs/ui`.

- Canonical Base UI wrapper: `libs/ui/src/components/ui/button.tsx`
- Canonical stepper: `libs/ui/src/components/ui/stepper.tsx` — no `CompactStepper` forks in apps

## Tokens in components

- **Lib components:** semantic tokens only (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `var(--primary)`).
- **Brand vars:** `--marrow-*`, `--dk-*` only in app CSS skins — never inside `libs/ui` TSX.

## Forms

- Labeled data-entry → `@f0rge/ui/forms` (Mantine wrappers).
- Apps never import Mantine directly.

## Submit / chrome

- `Button`, `Card`, `Dialog`, and other shadcn chrome from `@f0rge/ui`.
- Domain widgets stay in the app; do not promote app-specific UI into the kit without a deliberate primitive request.

## New primitives

1. Add under `libs/ui/src/components/ui/`.
2. Export from `libs/ui/src/index.ts`.
3. Add a Storybook story when `libs/ui/.storybook` exists.
4. **Never** copy shadcn into `apps/**/components/ui`.

Workflow skill: `.cursor/skills/add-ui-primitive/SKILL.md`.

## Catalogue

When Storybook is present, it is the source of truth:

```bash
npx nx run f0rge-ui:storybook
```

## Base UI vs Radix

`@f0rge/ui` runs on **Base UI**, not Radix. Use the `render` prop — not `asChild`:

```tsx
// WRONG
<DialogTrigger asChild><Button>Open</Button></DialogTrigger>

// CORRECT
<DialogTrigger render={<Button />}>Open</DialogTrigger>
```

`Select.onValueChange` may pass `null` — always null-guard.
